{
  "_comment": "Golden Collections, the importable Nuvio collections pack, as a tree: collection (a home row of tiles) > folder (a tile) > rows (named rows inside the folder page). Every folder row is served by this addon, so no other addon and no user API key is needed. Folder source fields: provider (streaming service key from providers.json, region-aware), network (TMDB network id, shows), company (TMDB company ids, pipe = OR), collection (TMDB franchise collection id), parts (a universe: {collections: [ids], movies: [ids]}, in release order), person (TMDB person id, the films they directed, from their credits), language (original language code), list (public MDBList JSON URL, per type), genre (TMDB genre id per type), keyword (TMDB keyword ids, pipe = OR), discover (explicit TMDB discover params per type), trending, group (ids of other folders: the tile opens one row per member, labelled with its name). Rows: each folder kind has default named rows (src/collections/facets.js PRESETS, e.g. Trending Movies, Top Rated Shows, Hidden Gems); rows [\"facet:type\"] overrides them. Optional: originals (TMDB network id, or {network, params}, of a streaming service own shows: the Original Series row), params (extra TMDB params), types (restrict to movie/series), regions (only show in these regions), indiaMix ([global, india] weights, or false to disable blending), tileShape. A collection with hidden: true (the library) is not shown; its folders exist only as group members. Genre, keyword, mood and curated folders blend Indian movies and series into every row (weights in providers.json indiaMix). All ids verified against TMDB on 2026-10-31.",
  "version": 4,
  "regionOrder": {
    "IN": ["spotlight", "streaming", "indian-cinema", "genres", "moods", "franchises", "studios", "world"],
    "_default": ["spotlight", "streaming", "genres", "moods", "franchises", "studios", "world", "indian-cinema"]
  },
